Week 05 Reflection

This week introduced VLANs and network segmentation. 
I configured VLANs on an OpenvSwitch to separate hosts into different broadcast domains.
I also learned how VLAN tagging works and how switches manage traffic between VLANs.
In the second task, I configured inter-VLAN routing using a Linux router with sub-interfaces. 
This showed how communication between VLANs is achieved.
The key takeaway was how VLANs improve network organisation, security, and efficiency.
I initially struggled with understanding trunk vs access ports, but testing configurations helped clarify the difference.
Next time, I will diagram the network before configuring VLANs to avoid confusion.
VLANs are widely used in organisations to separate departments securely, making this knowledge highly practical.
